---
.title = "Measure and Bound Work with Io Clock and Timeout",
.date = "2024-01-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

`std.Io.Clock` provides timestamps from a selected clock. `std.Io.Timeout` represents no timeout,
a duration, or a deadline; passing it to an operation bounds how long it may wait. This example
uses an awake-clock duration and measures the resulting wait.

